-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 113 and 114 -- A PROVINCE LEAVES THE PLAN; CHANGES THAT NEED THE PROVINCES' CONSENT.
-- Piece cp6, lines 2865 to 2882 and 3014 to 3034 of the Act file.
--
-- Section 113 says what follows when the Governor in Council prescribes a province under section 3(2) as one that has
-- assumed the plan's accrued obligations: those obligations stop being the Act's (113(1)(a)), the Minister of Finance pays the
-- province an amount in securities and cash (113(1)(b) and (2)), the Minister may call on the Investment Board for it (113(1.1)),
-- and may agree with the province on information and arrangements (113(3)).
-- Section 114 defines the "included provinces" and says that an Act of Parliament that changes the general level of benefits,
-- the classes of benefits, the contribution rates or the formulae takes effect only on a day fixed by order of the Governor in Council,
-- not earlier than the first day of the third year after notice of intention, and (for most changes) only with the consent of two thirds
-- of the included provinces having two thirds of their population.
--
-- THE TWO-THIRDS TEST is written once, under section 114(4), and called from section 113.1 (subsections (8.1), (11.145), (15)) and section 115(1.3).
-- THE JURAL RELATIONS: the person's liability to have a change in benefits or rates take effect only on the day the section fixes
-- (and the person's immunity from an earlier one), the provinces' power to block a change (their consent) and the federal government's
-- disability to bring it into force without it (s 114(2), (4)); the Minister of Finance's duty to pay the province and the province's
-- claim (s 113(1)(b)); the cessation of the Crown's liability for the accrued benefits the province has assumed (s 113(1)(a)), which is
-- the person's loss of a claim against the Act for those benefits (the province's plan now owes them).
--
-- Out of range, taken as inputs: the definition of "province providing a comprehensive pension plan" is the core's (cpp-core-application.l4);
-- the "designated securities" of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act and the manner of payment of the balance ("any manner that may be
-- prescribed"; no Regulation among the inputs prescribes one) are inputs.
-- Forks: C6-F15 how the territories are recognised in section 114(1); C6-F16 "any notice" in section 114(2); C6-F17 whether section 114(4) reaches a regulation.

§ `Part III -- a province leaves the plan, and changes needing the provinces' consent (sections 113 and 114)`

§§ `Section 113 -- effect of a regulation made under subsection 3(2)`

-- A regulation prescribing a province "as a province described in paragraph (b) of the definition province providing a comprehensive
-- pension plan" is a regulation under 3(2) after the province gave notice that it had provided by law for the plan and assumed the
-- obligations and liabilities accrued or accruing under this Act. The day the regulation becomes effective is the core's section 3(3).
-- src:2865 | Effect of regulation made under subsection 3(2)
-- src:2866 | 113 (1) Where any regulation has been made under subsection 3(2) prescribing a province as a province described in paragraph (b) of the definition province providing a comprehensive pension plan in subsection 3(1),
-- src:2867 | (a) all obligations and liabilities accrued or accruing as described in that paragraph, for the assumption of which under the provincial pension plan of that province provision has been made by any law of that province, shall, from and after the day on which the regulation became effective, cease to be obligations or liabilities accrued or accruing with respect to the payment of benefits under this Act attributable to contributions made under this Act in respect of employment in that province or in respect of self-employed earnings of persons resident in that province; and
@ref Act s 113(1)(a) (src:2865-2867)
GIVEN `a regulation has been made under subsection 3(2) prescribing the province as a province described in paragraph (b) of the definition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation or liability is one accrued or accruing as described in that paragraph, for the assumption of which provision has been made by a law of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation or liability is with respect to the payment of benefits attributable to contributions made under this Act in respect of employment in that province or in respect of self-employed earnings of persons resident in that province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the government of the province gave written notice` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113(1)(a) — the obligation or liability ceases to be one with respect to the payment of benefits under this Act` `a regulation has been made under subsection 3(2) prescribing the province as a province described in paragraph (b) of the definition` `the obligation or liability is one accrued or accruing as described in that paragraph, for the assumption of which provision has been made by a law of that province` `the obligation or liability is with respect to the payment of benefits attributable to contributions made under this Act in respect of employment in that province or in respect of self-employed earnings of persons resident in that province` `the date the government of the province gave written notice` day MEANS
        `a regulation has been made under subsection 3(2) prescribing the province as a province described in paragraph (b) of the definition`
    AND `the obligation or liability is one accrued or accruing as described in that paragraph, for the assumption of which provision has been made by a law of that province`
    AND `the obligation or liability is with respect to the payment of benefits attributable to contributions made under this Act in respect of employment in that province or in respect of self-employed earnings of persons resident in that province`
    -- "from and after the day on which the regulation became effective"
    AND day AT LEAST (`s 3(3) — the day a regulation under subsection (2) becomes effective` `the date the government of the province gave written notice`)

-- (b): the Minister of Finance pays the amount of subsection (2) "by the transfer to that government in the first instance and to the
-- extent necessary for that purpose, of securities of that province that are designated securities ..., and in the second instance and
-- to the extent necessary for that purpose, of securities of Canada that are designated securities ..., and by the payment to that
-- government of any balance then remaining in any manner that may be prescribed."
-- src:2868 | (b) the Minister of Finance shall pay an amount calculated as provided in subsection (2) to the government of that province, by the transfer to that government in the first instance and to the extent necessary for that purpose, of securities of that province that are designated securities as defined in section 2 of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act, and in the second instance and to the extent necessary for that purpose, of securities of Canada that are designated securities as defined in section 2 of that Act, and by the payment to that government of any balance then remaining in any manner that may be prescribed.
@ref Act s 113(1)(b) (src:2868)
GIVEN `the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the province's designated securities available for transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113(1)(b) — the value of the province's designated securities transferred in the first instance` `the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)` `the value of the province's designated securities available for transfer` MEANS
    min (max 0 `the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)`) (max 0 `the value of the province's designated securities available for transfer`)

@ref Act s 113(1)(b) (src:2868)
GIVEN `the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the province's designated securities available for transfer` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of Canada's designated securities available for transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113(1)(b) — the value of Canada's designated securities transferred in the second instance` `the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)` `the value of the province's designated securities available for transfer` `the value of Canada's designated securities available for transfer` MEANS
    min
        (max 0 ((`the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)`) MINUS (`s 113(1)(b) — the value of the province's designated securities transferred in the first instance` `the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)` `the value of the province's designated securities available for transfer`)))
        (max 0 `the value of Canada's designated securities available for transfer`)

-- Out of range: "any manner that may be prescribed"; no Regulation among the inputs prescribes one, so only the balance is computed.
@ref Act s 113(1)(b) (src:2868)
GIVEN `the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the province's designated securities available for transfer` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of Canada's designated securities available for transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113(1)(b) — the balance paid to the government of the province in a prescribed manner` `the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)` `the value of the province's designated securities available for transfer` `the value of Canada's designated securities available for transfer` MEANS
    max 0
        (((`the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)`)
            MINUS (`s 113(1)(b) — the value of the province's designated securities transferred in the first instance` `the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)` `the value of the province's designated securities available for transfer`))
            MINUS (`s 113(1)(b) — the value of Canada's designated securities transferred in the second instance` `the amount calculated under subsection 113(2)` `the value of the province's designated securities available for transfer` `the value of Canada's designated securities available for transfer`))

-- src:2869 | Transfer by Investment Board
-- src:2870 | (1.1) The Minister of Finance may, by notice, and in accordance with any agreement entered into under section 111.1, require the Investment Board to pay to that Minister any amount, and to transfer to that Minister any securities of the province or of Canada referred to in paragraph (1)(b), that are necessary for the purposes of subsection (1).
-- src:2871 | (1.2) [Repealed, 2003, c. 5, s. 9]
@ref Act s 113(1.1) (src:2869-2871)
GIVEN `the notice is in accordance with an agreement entered into under section 111.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount or securities are necessary for the purposes of subsection 113(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113(1.1) — the Minister of Finance may by notice require the Investment Board to pay the amount and transfer the securities` `the notice is in accordance with an agreement entered into under section 111.1` `the amount or securities are necessary for the purposes of subsection 113(1)` MEANS
    `the notice is in accordance with an agreement entered into under section 111.1` AND `the amount or securities are necessary for the purposes of subsection 113(1)`

-- Subsection 113(1.2) (line 2871) is repealed in this text and states nothing.

-- (2): the amount is (a) plus (b) less (c) less (d), where (d) is the part of the costs of administration equal to the
-- proportion that (a) is of the total contributions credited to the two accounts to that day.
-- NOTHING: the total contributions credited are zero, so the proportion in (d) is not defined.
-- src:2872 | Amount to be paid to government of province
-- src:2873 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the amount to be calculated as provided in this subsection in the case of any province shall be calculated by the Minister of Finance as the amount obtained by adding
-- src:2874 | (a) the total amount of all contributions credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account and the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account, to the day on which the regulation referred to in subsection (1) became effective, in respect of employment in that province or in respect of self-employed earnings of persons resident in that province, and
-- src:2875 | (b) the part of the net investment return of the Investment Board and all interest credited to or accrued to the credit of the Canada Pension Plan Account and the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account, to the day on which the regulation referred to in subsection (1) became effective, that is derived from the contributions referred to in paragraph (a),
-- src:2876 | and subtracting from the total so obtained
-- src:2877 | (c) such part of all amounts paid as or on account of benefits under this Act as would not have been payable under this Act if that province had been a province described in paragraph (a) of the definition province providing a comprehensive pension plan in subsection 3(1), and
-- src:2878 | (d) the part of the costs of administration of this Act, to the day on which the regulation referred to in subsection (1) became effective, that is equal to the proportion of those costs that the total amount of the contributions referred to in paragraph (a) is of the total amount of all contributions credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account and the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account to that day.
@ref Act s 113(2) (src:2872-2878)
GIVEN `the total amount of all contributions credited to the two accounts, to the day the regulation became effective, in respect of employment in that province or of self-employed earnings of persons resident in that province` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the net investment return of the Investment Board and of all interest credited or accrued to the two accounts, to that day, that is derived from those contributions` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of all amounts paid as or on account of benefits that would not have been payable if the province had been a province described in paragraph (a) of the definition` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs of administration of the Act to that day` IS A NUMBER
      `the total amount of all contributions credited to the two accounts to that day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 113(2) — the amount to be paid to the government of the province` `the total amount of all contributions credited to the two accounts, to the day the regulation became effective, in respect of employment in that province or of self-employed earnings of persons resident in that province` `the part of the net investment return of the Investment Board and of all interest credited or accrued to the two accounts, to that day, that is derived from those contributions` `the part of all amounts paid as or on account of benefits that would not have been payable if the province had been a province described in paragraph (a) of the definition` `the costs of administration of the Act to that day` `the total amount of all contributions credited to the two accounts to that day` MEANS
    IF `the total amount of all contributions credited to the two accounts to that day` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    (   (`the total amount of all contributions credited to the two accounts, to the day the regulation became effective, in respect of employment in that province or of self-employed earnings of persons resident in that province`)
                    PLUS (`the part of the net investment return of the Investment Board and of all interest credited or accrued to the two accounts, to that day, that is derived from those contributions`))
                MINUS (`the part of all amounts paid as or on account of benefits that would not have been payable if the province had been a province described in paragraph (a) of the definition`)
                -- (d): costs of administration times (a) over all contributions
                MINUS (   (`the costs of administration of the Act to that day`)
                       TIMES (   (`the total amount of all contributions credited to the two accounts, to the day the regulation became effective, in respect of employment in that province or of self-employed earnings of persons resident in that province`)
                              DIVIDED BY (`the total amount of all contributions credited to the two accounts to that day`))))

-- src:2879 | Agreement respecting assumption of obligations and liabilities
-- src:2880 | (3) Where notice in writing has been given to the Minister by the government of a province as described in the definition province providing a comprehensive pension plan in subsection 3(1), the Minister, with the approval of the Governor in Council, may on behalf of the Government of Canada enter into an agreement with the government of that province,
-- src:2881 | (a) for the furnishing of that government under prescribed conditions with any information obtained under this Act, including records of any amounts that are shown in the Record of Earnings to the accounts of persons who have made contributions under this Act in respect of employment in that province or as persons resident in that province in respect of self-employed earnings; and
-- src:2882 | (b) generally for the making of all such arrangements as may be necessary to permit provision to be made for the assumption, under the provincial pension plan referred to in the notice, of all obligations and liabilities accrued or accruing as described in paragraph (b) of the definition province providing a comprehensive pension plan in subsection 3(1).
@ref Act s 113(3) (src:2879-2882)
GIVEN `notice in writing has been given to the Minister by the government of the province as described in the definition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Governor in Council approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113(3) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the province` `notice in writing has been given to the Minister by the government of the province as described in the definition` `the Governor in Council approves` MEANS
    `notice in writing has been given to the Minister by the government of the province as described in the definition` AND `the Governor in Council approves`

§§ `Section 114 -- included provinces; changes that need notice and consent`

-- src:3015 | Amendments to Act
-- src:3016 | Definition of included province
-- src:3017 | 114 (1) In this section, included province means a province other than Yukon, the Northwest Territories or Nunavut, except a province providing a comprehensive pension plan unless at the time in respect of which the description is relevant there is in force an agreement entered into under subsection 4(3) with the government of that province.
@ref Act s 114(1) (src:3015-3017)
GIVEN province IS A Province
      `an agreement under subsection 4(3) with the government of that province is in force at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(1) — a province is an included province` province `an agreement under subsection 4(3) with the government of that province is in force at the time` MEANS
    -- "a province other than Yukon, the Northwest Territories or Nunavut", recognised by the names the text uses (fork C6-F15)
        NOT (   province's `name of the province` EQUALS "Yukon"
             OR province's `name of the province` EQUALS "the Northwest Territories"
             OR province's `name of the province` EQUALS "Nunavut")
    -- "except a province providing a comprehensive pension plan unless at the time ... there is in force an agreement entered into under
    -- subsection 4(3) with the government of that province"
    AND (   NOT province's `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`
         OR `an agreement under subsection 4(3) with the government of that province is in force at the time`)

-- The ways a change to benefits or contribution rates can come about, which decide which of subsections (2), (4) and (4.1)
-- (and section 113.1(12)) reach it. An enactment of Parliament is the case subsections (2) and (4) are written for.
DECLARE `cp6 Way a change to benefits or contribution rates comes about` IS ONE OF
    `an enactment of Parliament`
    `a regulation under subsection 113.1(6) amending Schedule 1 or 2`
    `a deemed amendment of Schedule 1 under subsections 113.1(11.05) to (11.11)`
    `a deemed amendment of Schedule 2 under subsection 113.1(11.141)`
    `a determination of the portions of benefits under subsection 113.1(11.142)`

-- src:3018 | Effective date of major amendments
-- src:3019 | (2) If any enactment of Parliament contains any provision that alters, or the effect of which is to alter, either directly or indirectly and either immediately or in the future, the general level of benefits provided by this Act or the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year, it shall be deemed to be a term of that enactment, whether or not it is expressly stated in the enactment, that the provision shall come into force only on a day to be fixed by order of the Governor in Council, which day shall not in any case be earlier than the first day of the third year following the year in which any notice of intention to introduce a measure containing a provision to that effect was laid before Parliament.
@ref Act s 114(2) (src:3018-3019)
GIVEN way IS A `cp6 Way a change to benefits or contribution rates comes about`
      `the provision alters the general level of benefits provided by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision alters the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(2) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(2)` way `the provision alters the general level of benefits provided by the Act` `the provision alters the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year` MEANS
    -- "either directly or indirectly and either immediately or in the future": not conditions, so not inputs.
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `an enactment of Parliament` THEN
        `the provision alters the general level of benefits provided by the Act`
        OR `the provision alters the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year`
    -- subsection 113.1(12) and subsection 114(4.1) take every other way out of subsection (2)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "the first day of the third year following the year in which any notice of intention ... was laid before Parliament": a notice laid
-- in 2026 has 2027, 2028 and 2029 as the years following, so the first day of the third is 1 January 2029. The core reads section 3(3),
-- "the first day of the third year following the year in which the notice ... was given", the same way.
-- "any notice": one notice is taken (fork C6-F16).
@ref Act s 114(2) (src:3018-3019)
GIVEN `the year in which the notice of intention was laid before Parliament` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 114(2) — the earliest day on which the provision may come into force` `the year in which the notice of intention was laid before Parliament` MEANS
    YearMonthDay ((`the year in which the notice of intention was laid before Parliament`) PLUS 3) 1 1

-- NOTHING: the provision is not within subsection (2), which then says nothing about when it may come into force.
@ref Act s 114(2) (src:3018-3019)
GIVEN way IS A `cp6 Way a change to benefits or contribution rates comes about`
      `the provision alters the general level of benefits provided by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision alters the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year in which the notice of intention was laid before Parliament` IS A NUMBER
      `the day is fixed by order of the Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114(2) — the provision may come into force on a day` way `the provision alters the general level of benefits provided by the Act` `the provision alters the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year` `the year in which the notice of intention was laid before Parliament` `the day is fixed by order of the Governor in Council` day MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 114(2) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(2)` way `the provision alters the general level of benefits provided by the Act` `the provision alters the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `the day is fixed by order of the Governor in Council`
               AND day AT LEAST (`s 114(2) — the earliest day on which the provision may come into force` `the year in which the notice of intention was laid before Parliament`))

-- src:3020 | Notice
-- src:3021 | (3) A notice of intention described in subsection (2) shall be in such form as is sufficient to indicate the nature of the provision contained or proposed to be contained in the measure referred to in subsection (2) to the effect described in that subsection, and on any such notice being laid before Parliament the Minister shall forthwith cause a copy thereof to be sent to the lieutenant governor in council of each included province.
@ref Act s 114(3) (src:3020-3021)
GIVEN `the notice is in such form as is sufficient to indicate the nature of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(3) — the notice of intention is in the form the subsection requires` `the notice is in such form as is sufficient to indicate the nature of the provision` MEANS
    `the notice is in such form as is sufficient to indicate the nature of the provision`

@ref Act s 114(3) (src:3020-3021)
GIVEN `the notice described in subsection 114(2) has been laid before Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(3) — the Minister must forthwith cause a copy of the notice to be sent to the lieutenant governor in council of each included province` `the notice described in subsection 114(2) has been laid before Parliament` MEANS
    `the notice described in subsection 114(2) has been laid before Parliament`

-- (4): "(a) the general level of benefits ...; (b) the classes of benefits ...; (c) the contribution rate, first additional contribution
-- rate or second additional contribution rate ...; (d) the formulae for calculating the contributions and benefits payable ...; (e) the
-- management or operation of the Canada Pension Plan Account or the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account, or (f) the Canada Pension Plan
-- Investment Board Act".
