-- src:3023 | (4) Where any enactment of Parliament contains any provision that alters, or the effect of which is to alter, either directly or indirectly and either immediately or in the future,
-- src:3024 | (a) the general level of benefits provided by this Act,
-- src:3025 | (b) the classes of benefits provided by this Act,
-- src:3026 | (c) the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year,
-- src:3027 | (d) the formulae for calculating the contributions and benefits payable under this Act,
-- src:3028 | (e) the management or operation of the Canada Pension Plan Account or the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account, or
-- src:3029 | (f) the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act,
-- src:3030 | it shall be deemed to be a term of that enactment, whether or not it is expressly stated in the enactment, that the provision shall come into force only on a day to be fixed by order of the Governor in Council, which order may not be made and shall not in any case have any force or effect unless the lieutenant governor in council of each of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having in the aggregate not less than two thirds of the population of all of the included provinces, has signified the consent of that province to the enactment.
@ref Act s 114(4) (src:3022-3030)
DECLARE `cp6 Matter an enactment of Parliament alters for subsection 114(4)` IS ONE OF
    `the general level of benefits provided by the Act`
    `the classes of benefits provided by the Act`
    `the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year`
    `the formulae for calculating the contributions and benefits payable under the Act`
    `the management or operation of the Canada Pension Plan Account or the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account`
    `the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act`
    `some other matter`

-- NOTHING: the text does not say whether subsection (4) reaches a regulation under subsection 113.1(6) (fork C6-F17): it speaks of
-- "any enactment of Parliament", and neither subsection (4.1) nor 113.1(12) mentions (4) for a regulation.
@ref Act s 114(4) (src:3022-3030)
GIVEN way IS A `cp6 Way a change to benefits or contribution rates comes about`
      matter IS A `cp6 Matter an enactment of Parliament alters for subsection 114(4)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` way matter MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `an enactment of Parliament` THEN
        CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `some other matter` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a regulation under subsection 113.1(6) amending Schedule 1 or 2` THEN NOTHING
    -- subsection (4.1): changes under 113.1(11.05) to (11.11), (11.141) or (11.142) are outside subsections (2) and (4)
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- The two-thirds test of subsections 114(4), 113.1(8.1), 113.1(11.145), 113.1(15) and 115(1.3): "the lieutenant governor in council of each of
-- at least two thirds of the included provinces, having in the aggregate not less than two thirds of the population of all of the
-- included provinces, has signified the consent of that province". Written with whole numbers: three times the part is not less
-- than twice the whole.
@ref Act s 114(4) (src:3022-3030)
GIVEN `the number of included provinces` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of included provinces whose lieutenant governor in council has signified consent` IS A NUMBER
      `the population of all the included provinces` IS A NUMBER
      `the population of the included provinces that have signified consent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(4) — the consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` `the number of included provinces` `the number of included provinces whose lieutenant governor in council has signified consent` `the population of all the included provinces` `the population of the included provinces that have signified consent` MEANS
        ((`the number of included provinces whose lieutenant governor in council has signified consent`) TIMES 3) AT LEAST ((`the number of included provinces`) TIMES 2)
    AND ((`the population of the included provinces that have signified consent`) TIMES 3) AT LEAST ((`the population of all the included provinces`) TIMES 2)

-- "which order may not be made and shall not in any case have any force or effect unless" consent has been signified.
-- NOTHING: the provision is not within subsection (4) (or the text does not say whether it is).
@ref Act s 114(4) (src:3022-3030)
GIVEN way IS A `cp6 Way a change to benefits or contribution rates comes about`
      matter IS A `cp6 Matter an enactment of Parliament alters for subsection 114(4)`
      `consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114(4) — the order fixing the day for the provision may be made and has force` way matter `consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` way matter
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST subject THEN
        IF subject
        THEN JUST `consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified`
        ELSE NOTHING

-- (4.1): "Subsections (2) and (4) do not apply in respect of changes under any of subsections 113.1(11.05) to (11.11), (11.141) or (11.142)
-- to benefits, contribution rates, first additional contribution rates or second additional contribution rates."
-- src:3031 | Exception
-- src:3032 | (4.1) Subsections (2) and (4) do not apply in respect of changes under any of subsections 113.1(11.05) to (11.11), (11.141) or (11.142) to benefits, contribution rates, first additional contribution rates or second additional contribution rates.
@ref Act s 114(4.1) (src:3031-3032)
GIVEN way IS A `cp6 Way a change to benefits or contribution rates comes about`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 114(4.1) — subsections 114(2) and (4) do not apply to the change` way MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `a deemed amendment of Schedule 1 under subsections 113.1(11.05) to (11.11)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a deemed amendment of Schedule 2 under subsection 113.1(11.141)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a determination of the portions of benefits under subsection 113.1(11.142)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an enactment of Parliament` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a regulation under subsection 113.1(6) amending Schedule 1 or 2` THEN FALSE

-- Section 113.1(12) (line 3004-3005): "For greater certainty, subsection 114(2) does not apply to any amendment to Schedule 1 or 2 made under
-- subsection (6), (11.05) to (11.11) or (11.141)." Written here, beside the subsection it limits.
-- src:3004 | Non-application of subsection 114(2)
-- src:3005 | (12) For greater certainty, subsection 114(2) does not apply to any amendment to Schedule 1 or 2 made under subsection (6), (11.05) to (11.11) or (11.141).
@ref Act s 113.1(12) (src:3004-3005)
GIVEN way IS A `cp6 Way a change to benefits or contribution rates comes about`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(12) — subsection 114(2) does not apply to the amendment of Schedule 1 or 2` way MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `a regulation under subsection 113.1(6) amending Schedule 1 or 2` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a deemed amendment of Schedule 1 under subsections 113.1(11.05) to (11.11)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a deemed amendment of Schedule 2 under subsection 113.1(11.141)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a determination of the portions of benefits under subsection 113.1(11.142)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an enactment of Parliament` THEN FALSE

-- src:3033 | Determination of population
-- src:3034 | (5) For the purposes of this section, the population of a province at any time in a year in respect of which the determination thereof is relevant means the population thereof on June 1 of that year, as estimated by the Chief Statistician of Canada.
@ref Act s 114(5) (src:3033-3034)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 114(5) — the day on which the population of a province is taken for a year` year MEANS
    YearMonthDay year 6 1
